@ 36.3.3.1 - Old Tibetan to Amdo dialects
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Jacques, Guillaume (2004), “Phonologie et Morphologie du Japhug (rGyalrong)”. Université Paris-Diderot – Paris VII <tel-00138568>. NB: This source is in French and looks to at least sometimes use a transcription that isn’t IPA.
	{d,ɡ,s,l,r} > {h,r} / #_
	ʃ > x / #_ (some dialect͡s, never when following preinitials)
	{ k(ʰ){r,j}, ɡ{r,j} } > { t͡ɕ(ʰ), d͡ʑ }
	{ pʰ, b } > { h, w }
	i > ə / _#
	sr > ʂ / #_
	s > either i or a diphthong ending in i? / _#
	d > l / _# (some dialect͡s)
	t > l / _# (further development in bLa-brang)